# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what you have.
# `.env` is gitignored; this example is not, so never put a real value here.
#
# An exported environment variable takes priority over anything in `.env`.

# Optional. Adds Discogs as a cover source for pressings a commercial
# catalogue skips — obscure releases, vinyl, special editions.
# Generate one at https://www.discogs.com/settings/developers
LYRICA_DISCOGS_TOKEN=

# Optional. Lets the overlay work out which YouTube video is playing, so it can
# find where the song starts in one that opens with an intro and stop the lyrics
# running early. Windows does not publish the video's identity, so it is
# recovered by searching for the title and keeping the result whose length
# matches. Without a key nothing here happens and `Enter` still corrects an
# intro by hand.
# Create one at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/youtube.googleapis.com
# (YouTube Data API v3). The free allowance is about a hundred lookups a day,
# and each answer is cached for a month.
LYRICA_YOUTUBE_KEY=

# Optional. Moves the lyrics cache somewhere synchronised between machines.
# LYRICA_CACHE_DIR=C:\Users\you\OneDrive\Lyrica\cache

# Optional. How big the overlay is drawn, as a multiple of its designed size.
# Multiplies into the display scale, so window, text, cover, gaps and fade
# bands all move together. Allowed range 0.6 to 2.0; anything outside is
# clamped, anything unparseable is ignored.
# LYRICA_SIZE=1.25

# Optional. How solid the panel is, 0.6 to 1.0. Lower shows more of whatever is
# behind it. Anything outside the range is clamped.
# LYRICA_OPACITY=0.90

# Optional. How wide the sweep's leading edge is, in pixels — the band where a
# letter is part-way between sung and unsung. A letter is about 18 wide, so 40
# keeps two and a half letters in transition and reads as a cloud; 16 keeps one
# and reads as an edge. Under about 10 the transition is shorter than a frame at
# fast delivery and narrowing it further changes nothing. Range 4 to 60.
# LYRICA_SWEEP_FEATHER=12

# Optional. How long a sung word keeps its light, as a multiple of how long
# that word is sung for. One means the light drains exactly as the word
# finishes. Not seconds: the sweep crossing a word is already on the word's own
# clock, and a fixed number put the two in disagreement. `off` removes it.
# Range 0 to 3.
# LYRICA_BLOOM=1.0

# Optional. How much larger a struck word gets, as a fraction. `off` removes
# the growth and leaves the light. Range 0 to 0.35. It has a floor that is not
# taste: below about 0.10 several steps of the growth render to the same
# whole-pixel size and a third of its frames show an identical picture.
# LYRICA_GROWTH=0.14

# Optional. How the border reacts to what is playing.
#   comet  a bright head travelling a dark ring
#   shine  the whole border lit, with a gradient rotating through it (the default)
#   off    no border effect
# LYRICA_BEAM=shine
